 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the issuance of a\ndistinctive license plate for members of the New York state Elks association\nof the benevolent and protective order of the Elks",
    "basePrintNo": "S8869",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8869-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-z, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8869\n\nSPONSOR: AMEDORE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the issuance\nof a distinctive license plate for members of the New York state Elks\nassociation of the benevolent and protective order of the Elks\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would allow members of the New York State Elks to\nobtain a distinctive license plate that bears special wording that\nrecognizes both the organization and the membership of the applicant.\nThe act authorizes verification by the Commissioner of the Department of\nMotor Vehicles that the motorist has an active membership with the Elks.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. The vehicle and traffic Law is amended by adding a new\nsection 404-z\n\n1. Establishing that members of the New York State Elks Association of\nthe Benevolent and Protective Order of the Elks, upon request, shall be\nissued a license plate bearing the words \"Elks Association.\"\n\n2. Requires that satisfactory proof of membership be presented to the\nDepartment.\n\n3. Establishes that the plate will be issued in the same manner as other\nnumbered license plates upon the payment of the regular registration fee\nand annual service charge of twenty-five dollars.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, The State of New York makes available many different distinc-\ntive license plates to members of various groups. The New York State\nElks Association of the Benevolent and Protective Order of the Elks is a\ncommunity organization whose members take pride in their patriotic spir-\nit and commitment to serving their communities. This legislation would\nmake it possible for proud members of this organization to show their\naffiliation with the Elks by displaying a distinctive New York State\nlicense plate.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Senate bill.\n\n2013-14: A.9010 - referred to Transportation\n2015-16: A2517 - referred to Transportation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
